{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Data Accessibility", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when talking about data accessibility.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations. Understand information about data and its structure in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "There is \u2013 There are / How much? \u2013 How Many with Countable and Uncountable Nouns", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <strong>there is - there are</strong> to express the existence of something<br/> You use<strong> How much \u2013 How many</strong>  to ask for the existence of something<br/>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use <strong>there is</strong> with singular nouns or uncountable nouns that are the ones you cannot count unless you have a specific unit of amount.<br/><br/>   Use the following structure:<br/><br/>  There is + singular noun   / There is + uncountable nouns<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><br/>Example:<br/> <span class=\"strong\">There is</span> a database that includes all the information. <br/><span class=\"strong\">There is</span> information on data accessibility.</span><br/><br/>  Uncountable nouns are always singularm, so you use <span class=\"strong\"> \u201chow much\u201d </span> to ask for a particular amount, following this structure:<br/><br/>  How much + uncountable noun + complement +? <span class=\"italic\"><br/>For example: <strong>How much</strong> money do you need to store data?</span><br/><br/>  On the other hand, you use<strong> there are</strong> with plural or countable nouns, using the following structure:<br/><br/>  There are + plural nouns / There are + countable nouns<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Example: <strong>There are</strong> three programmers working on database access.</span><br/><br/>  Countable nouns are always plural, so you use <span class=\"strong\"> \u201cHow many\u201d </span> to ask for a specific quantity, following this structure:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">How many + countable noun + complement +?<br/> For example: <br/><strong>How many</strong> assistances do you need to store data?</span><br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There is something important to discuss.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How many representatives do you need?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Betty, how much time do you need to send an email to all our representatives?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are different things that we have to take into consideration.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How many aspects are there?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How many facts are there in accessibility?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How much time an effort it is necessary to accomplish that?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How many procedures the organization need to restore data?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are just two procedures.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Present Continuous for Plans in Affirmative", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <strong>present continuous<strong/> to describe plans or events you have for a near future.<br/>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use present continuous for plans in a near future using the same affirmative structure:<br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Subject + Verb To Be (am- are \u2013 is) + Verb- ing + Complement</strong></span><br/><br />   Don't forget to use the verb <span class=\"strong\">Be</span> according to the subject .<br /><br /> I   -   <span class=\"strong\">am</span><br />You   -   <span class=\"strong\">are</span><br />He-She-It   -  <span class=\"strong\">is</span><br />We   -  <span class=\"strong\">are</span><br />They   -   <span class=\"strong\">are</span><br /> <span class=\"italic\"><br/><br />Example: She <strong>is planning</strong> a meeting tomorrow to talk about data accessibility. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I am planning a meeting to talk to the CEO, but I need some help.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Sir, representatives are receiving an invitation to come.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We are planning to explain data accessibility as those activities we relate to storing and creating reliable databases.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We are planning to explain data accessibility as those activities we relate to storing and creating reliable databases.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The company is acquiring a robust system that is reliable, we are also mirroring the database on multiple servers; and we are planning to create a backup of all the information we are storing and updating concurrently.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Search information about data accessibility.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a conversation where you explain the definition of data accessibility.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include how many processes there are in accessibility.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe how much time do you need to accomplish those processes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "List main plans you are doing for a new future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your conversation to check spelling. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your conversation with your instructor and one classmate. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I search information about data accessibility.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I identify the definition of data accessibility", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I recognize some main facts about data accessibility.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I list processes in data accessibility.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "data queries ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "requests of information from a database", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Well, there are five assistants who can help me to check the data queries.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "e-commerce ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "online application for storing information", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Assistants are working on the availability of information; they are using from next month an e-commerce application, so they are having updated information 24 hours, 7 days a week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "concurrently", "type": "name"}, {"content": "at the same time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We are planning to create a backup of all the information we are storing and updating concurrently.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "backup", "t